{
  "info": {
    "name": "IAM Service — User API",
    "_postman_id": "b6f6b1f0-8b3a-4b1e-9b0e-iam-users-0001",
    "description": "Exercises every /api/v1/users endpoint implemented in app/api/v1/routes/users.py, plus the minimal auth/org/role scaffolding needed to reach them.\n\n**Prerequisites (do these once, outside Postman):**\n1. Run the service: `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000`.\n2. Create a superuser (no HTTP endpoint can bootstrap the first one):\n   `uv run python scripts/create_superuser.py admin@example.com ChangeMe123!`\n   Update the `superuser_email` / `superuser_password` collection variables if you used different values.\n3. (Optional, only needed for the \"4. Permissions\" folder) Seed the platform permission catalog — there is no HTTP endpoint for this either:\n   ```\n   uv run python3 -c \"\n   import asyncio\n   from app.infrastructure.db.session import async_session_factory\n   from app.services.rbac_seed import seed_rbac_catalog\n   async def main():\n       async with async_session_factory() as s:\n           await seed_rbac_catalog(s)\n           await s.commit()\n   asyncio.run(main())\n   \"\n   ```\n\n**Auto token handling:**\n- Every Login/Register request's *Test* script captures `access_token`/`refresh_token`/the user's `id` into collection variables for that actor (`member_*`, `superuser_*`) — no manual copy/paste between requests.\n- A **collection-level pre-request script** runs before every request below: it decodes the relevant actor's stored access token, and if it's missing or within 5 seconds of expiring, transparently calls `POST /auth/refresh` and overwrites the stored token before the actual request fires. So you can leave this running (e.g. via Collection Runner) past a token's lifetime without it ever 401ing on expiry.\n- Re-running the whole collection is safe: emails/usernames/org slugs are suffixed with `Date.now()` in pre-request scripts so nothing collides with a previous run.\n\nRun order matters: folders are numbered and build on each other (Setup creates the org + actors that later folders mutate). Use Collection Runner or run folders top-to-bottom.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level: auto-detect a near-expired/missing access token for",
          "// the current actor(s) and silently refresh it via POST /auth/refresh",
          "// before the request runs, so nothing below ever has to manually",
          "// re-paste a token after it expires.",
          "function base64UrlDecode(input) {",
          "    input = input.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');",
          "    while (input.length % 4) { input += '='; }",
          "    return decodeURIComponent(",
          "        atob(input).split('').map(function (c) {",
          "            return '%' + ('00' + c.charCodeAt(0).toString(16)).slice(-2);",
          "        }).join('')",
          "    );",
          "}",
          "",
          "function isExpiredOrMissing(token) {",
          "    if (!token) return true;",
          "    var parts = token.split('.');",
          "    if (parts.length !== 3) return true;",
          "    try {",
          "        var payload = JSON.parse(base64UrlDecode(parts[1]));",
          "        return !payload.exp || (payload.exp * 1000) < (Date.now() + 5000);",
          "    } catch (e) {",
          "        return true;",
          "    }",
          "}",
          "",
          "function refreshActor(actor, cb) {",
          "    var accessVar = actor + '_access_token';",
          "    var refreshVar = actor + '_refresh_token';",
          "    var accessToken = pm.collectionVariables.get(accessVar);",
          "    var refreshToken = pm.collectionVariables.get(refreshVar);",
          "",
          "    if (!refreshToken || !isExpiredOrMissing(accessToken)) {",
          "        return cb();",
          "    }",
          "",
          "    pm.sendRequest({",
          "        url: pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url') + '/api/v1/auth/refresh',",
          "        method: 'POST',",
          "        header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
          "        body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ refresh_token: refreshToken }) }",
          "    }, function (err, res) {",
          "        if (!err && res && res.code === 200) {",
          "            var json = res.json();",
          "            pm.collectionVariables.set(accessVar, json.access_token);",
          "            pm.collectionVariables.set(refreshVar, json.refresh_token);",
          "            console.log('[auto-refresh] ' + actor + ' access token refreshed');",
          "        } else {",
          "            console.log('[auto-refresh] ' + actor + ' refresh skipped/failed (continuing with existing token)');",
          "        }",
          "        cb();",
          "    });",
          "}",
          "",
          "// The Setup folder's own Login/Register/Refresh requests establish or",
          "// rotate tokens directly via their own Test scripts below — skip",
          "// auto-refresh for those so we don't step on a request whose whole",
          "// job is defining the token.",
          "var requestName = pm.info.requestName || '';",
          "if (!/^(Login|Register|Refresh)/i.test(requestName)) {",
          "    refreshActor('member', function () {",
          "        refreshActor('superuser', function () {});",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8000" },
    { "key": "superuser_email", "value": "admin@example.com" },
    { "key": "superuser_password", "value": "ChangeMe123!" },
    { "key": "superuser_access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "superuser_refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "superuser_user_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_email", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_password", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_user_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "org_name", "value": "" },
    { "key": "org_slug", "value": "" },
    { "key": "organization_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "member_role_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "admin_role_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "guest_role_id", "value": "" },
